From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iwanicki92 <iwanicki92@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 22:48:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] loader/i386/linux: clear the real-mode chunk before filling
 the zero page

The kernel takes the whole 4 KiB zero page and a dynamic launch
measures all of it as "Measured boot parameters", while linux_params
covers only the first 0x3fc bytes. The rest of the page was whatever
the relocator chunk held, GRUB heap contents that vary with the
command line's length, so two launches differing only in a kernel
parameter got different PCR 18 boot params digests.

Zero the chunk right after it is allocated, the way the SKINIT setup
already zeros the MLE for stable measurements.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: iwanicki92 <iwanicki92@gmail.com>
---
 grub-core/loader/i386/linux.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/grub-core/loader/i386/linux.c b/grub-core/loader/i386/linux.c
index f5b13c2..38a65d4 100644
--- a/grub-core/loader/i386/linux.c
+++ b/grub-core/loader/i386/linux.c
@@ -595,6 +595,13 @@ grub_linux_boot (void)
      return err;
     real_mode_mem = get_virtual_current_address (ch);
 
+    /*
+     * The kernel takes the whole 4 KiB zero page and a dynamic launch
+     * measures it, while linux_params fills less than that: clear the
+     * chunk so the rest is not whatever memory held before.
+     */
+    grub_memset (real_mode_mem, 0, sz);
+
     if (grub_slaunch_platform_type () != SLP_NONE)
       {
         slparams.boot_params = real_mode_mem;
-- 
